IMPORT thread

' bug-482: each entry below declares an `In` parameter that is NOT
' thread-sendable per spec §16. The entries themselves are well-formed —
' the defect being pinned is that `thread::start`'s call-site check on the
' `data` argument never fired, so a caller could hand any of these a value
' that must not cross the boundary.

' A function value. A capturing lambda passed here would have its closure
' environment read from the PARENT's arena on the worker thread.
EXPORT ISOLATED FUNC takesFunc(t AS ThreadWorker OF Nothing TO Integer, f AS FUNC() AS Integer) AS Integer
  RETURN f()
END FUNC

' A thread handle. `Thread` is non-sendable: a handle is meaningful only on
' the thread that owns it.
EXPORT ISOLATED FUNC takesHandle(t AS ThreadWorker OF Nothing TO Integer, h AS Thread OF Nothing TO Integer) AS Integer
  RETURN 1
END FUNC

' The sendable control case: an Integer `In` must keep compiling clean, so
' the fixture proves the rule narrowed to non-sendable types rather than
' rejecting every `thread::start`.
EXPORT ISOLATED FUNC takesInteger(t AS ThreadWorker OF Nothing TO Integer, n AS Integer) AS Integer
  RETURN n
END FUNC
